-- **PSRAM Dual Framebuffers**: Allocate 2 full framebuffers in PSRAM (`.fb_in_psram = 1`) for 800x480 RGB565 display (~1.5 MB total).
+- **PSRAM Framebuffer**: framebuffers live in PSRAM (`.fb_in_psram = 1`); their count comes from `esp_lv_adapter_get_required_frame_buffer_count()`. `src/main.c` picks `ESP_LV_ADAPTER_TEAR_AVOID_MODE_NONE` (single buffer, partial refresh) so drawing does not starve the PSRAM bus while Wi-Fi is active — the reason is in the comment in `app_main`.
+- **LVGL Heap**: LVGL's built-in allocator uses a fixed pool, `CONFIG_LV_MEM_SIZE_KILOBYTES` (128 KB in `sdkconfig.defaults`). Running out hits `LV_ASSERT_MALLOC`, which hangs. `host_sim` prints the usage after UI init (`[sim] lvgl heap after UI init`) and its stress test fails below 30% free — re-check after adding widgets.
 - **Internal SRAM Bounce Buffer**: Allocate a 40-line internal SRAM bounce buffer (`bounce_buffer_size_px = 800 * 40`) to prevent PSRAM bus starvation and LCD flickering during simultaneous Wi-Fi/MQTT activities.
